  "contentHtml": "\n\t\t\t\t\t\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A </span><b>Work Permit in UAE</b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> is a legal document that allows foreign nationals to work in the United Arab Emirates. Since the UAE attracts professionals from around the world, the government has strict rules to regulate employment and protect workers. Anyone who wants to work in the country must obtain a valid </span><a href=\"/visa-services/employment-visa\"><b>UAE employment visa</b></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> and work permit through an employer.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Working on a tourist visa is illegal and can lead to fines, visa cancellation, or deportation. To work legally, employees must go through a formal process that includes labour approval, an entry permit, a residence visa, and an Emirates ID.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The process is mainly regulated by the Ministry of Human Resources and Emiratisation (MOHRE) and the Federal Authority for Identity, Citizenship, Customs and Port Security (ICP). These authorities ensure that both employers and employees follow the official </span><b>UAE work visa requirements</b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.</span></p>\n<div class=\"lwptoc lwptoc-autoWidth lwptoc-baseItems lwptoc-light lwptoc-notInherit\" data-smooth-scroll=\"1\" data-smooth-scroll-offset=\"24\"><div class=\"lwptoc_i\">    <div class=\"lwptoc_header\">\n        <b class=\"lwptoc_title\">Contents</b>                    <span class=\"lwptoc_toggle\">\n                <a href=\"#\" class=\"lwptoc_toggle_label\" data-label=\"show\">hide</a>            </span>\n            </div>\n<div class=\"lwptoc_items lwptoc_items-visible\">\n    <div class=\"lwptoc_itemWrap\"><div class=\"lwptoc_item\">    <a href=\"#What_is_a_Work_Permit_in_UAE\">\n                <span class=\"lwptoc_item_label\">What is a Work Permit in UAE?</span>\n    </a>\n    </div><div class=\"lwptoc_item\">    <a href=\"#Work_Permit_vs_Employment_Visa_in_UAE\">\n                <span class=\"lwptoc_item_label\">Work Permit vs Employment Visa in UAE</span>\n    </a>\n    </div><div class=\"lwptoc_item\">    <a href=\"#Types_of_Work_Permits_in_UAE\">\n                <span class=\"lwptoc_item_label\">Types of Work Permits in UAE</span>\n    </a>\n    </div><div class=\"lwptoc_item\">    <a href=\"#Eligibility_Criteria_for_UAE_Work_Permit\">\n                <span class=\"lwptoc_item_label\">Eligibility Criteria for UAE Work Permit</span>\n    </a>\n    </div><div class=\"lwptoc_item\">    <a href=\"#Documents_Required_for_Work_Permit_in_UAE\">\n                <span class=\"lwptoc_item_label\">Documents Required for Work Permit in UAE</span>\n    </a>\n    </div><div class=\"lwptoc_item\">    <a href=\"#Step-by-Step_Process_to_Apply_for_Work_Permit_in_UAE\">\n                <span class=\"lwptoc_item_label\">Step-by-Step Process to Apply for Work Permit in UAE</span>\n    </a>\n    </div><div class=\"lwptoc_item\">    <a href=\"#Work_Permit_Cost_in_UAE\">\n                <span class=\"lwptoc_item_label\">Work Permit Cost in UAE</span>\n    </a>\n    </div><div class=\"lwptoc_item\">    <a href=\"#Processing_Time_for_UAE_Work_Permit\">\n                <span class=\"lwptoc_item_label\">Processing Time for UAE Work Permit</span>\n    </a>\n    </div><div class=\"lwptoc_item\">    <a href=\"#Free_Zone_vs_Mainland_Work_Permits\">\n                <span class=\"lwptoc_item_label\">Free Zone vs Mainland Work Permits</span>\n    </a>\n    </div><div class=\"lwptoc_item\">    <a href=\"#How_to_Renew_or_Cancel_a_UAE_Work_Permit\">\n                <span class=\"lwptoc_item_label\">How to Renew or Cancel a UAE Work Permit</span>\n    </a>\n    </div><div class=\"lwptoc_item\">    <a href=\"#Benefits_of_Having_a_UAE_Work_Permit\">\n                <span class=\"lwptoc_item_label\">Benefits of Having a UAE Work Permit</span>\n    </a>\n    </div><div class=\"lwptoc_item\">    <a href=\"#Common_Reasons_for_Work_Permit_Rejection\">\n                <span class=\"lwptoc_item_label\">Common Reasons for Work Permit Rejection</span>\n    </a>\n    </div><div class=\"lwptoc_item\">    <a href=\"#FAQs_About_Work_Permit_in_UAE\">\n                <span class=\"lwptoc_item_label\">FAQs About Work Permit in UAE</span>\n    </a>\n    </div></div></div>\n</div></div><h2 id=\"what-is-a-work-permit-in-uae\"><b>What is a Work Permit in UAE?</b></h2>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A </span><b>UAE work permit</b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> is an official authorization issued by the government that allows a foreign national to work legally in the country. It is an essential part of the </span><b>employment visa UAE</b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> process.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">In simple terms, the work permit confirms that the employee is legally hired by a UAE company and is allowed to perform a specific job role.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The permit is usually sponsored by the employer, meaning the company takes responsibility for hiring the worker and completing the required government procedures.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The main authority responsible for issuing work permits is the Ministry of Human Resources and Emiratisation. The ministry regulates employment contracts, protects worker rights, and ensures companies follow labour laws.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Without a valid work permit, foreign workers cannot legally work in the UAE.</span></p>\n<p><img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter size-large wp-image-9965\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Work-permit-in-UAE-e1773654696774-1024x457.webp\" alt=\"Work permit in UAE\" width=\"1024\" height=\"457\"><noscript><img fetchpriority=\"high\" fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter size-large wp-image-9965\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Work-permit-in-UAE-e1773654696774-1024x457.webp\" alt=\"Work permit in UAE\" width=\"1024\" height=\"457\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Work-permit-in-UAE-e1773654696774-1024x457.webp 1024w, /wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Work-permit-in-UAE-e1773654696774-300x134.webp 300w, /wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Work-permit-in-UAE-e1773654696774-768x343.webp 768w, /wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Work-permit-in-UAE-e1773654696774-1536x686.webp 1536w, /wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Work-permit-in-UAE-e1773654696774.webp 1848w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\"></noscript></p>\n<h2 id=\"work-permit-vs-employment-visa-in-uae\"><b>Work Permit vs Employment Visa in UAE</b></h2>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Many people think a work permit and an employment visa are the same. However, they are different documents that work together in the UAE immigration system.</span></p>\n<h3 id=\"work-permit\"><b>Work Permit</b></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A </span><b>work permit</b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> is issued by the labour authority.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">It allows the employer to legally hire a foreign worker. </span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">This permit is approved by the Ministry of Human Resources and Emiratisation and confirms the job offer.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"entry-permit\"><b>Entry Permit</b></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">An </span><b>entry permit</b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> allows the employee to enter the UAE for employment purposes. </span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">This document is usually issued before the employee travels to the country. It is approved by the Federal Authority for Identity, Citizenship, Customs, and Port Security.</span></p>\n<h3 id=\"residence-visa\"><b>Residence Visa</b></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The </span><a href=\"/uae-residence-visa/\"><b>residence visa</b></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> allows the worker to stay and work in the UAE long-term. </span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Once the residence visa is issued, the employee receives an Emirates ID and becomes a legal resident. </span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">In short, the work permit allows employment, while the residence visa allows legal stay in the country.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"types-of-work-permits-in-uae\"><b>Types of Work Permits in UAE</b></h2>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The UAE government offers several </span><b>UAE work permit types</b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> depending on the nature of employment. These permits are mainly issued under the regulations of the Ministry of Human Resources and Emiratisation.</span></p>\n<h3 id=\"standard-employment-work-permit\"><b>Standard Employment Work Permit</b></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">This is the most common type of permit in the UAE. </span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">It is issued to employees working for mainland companies and is sponsored by the employer. The permit usually comes with a </span><b>2-year residence visa</b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.</span></p>\n<h3 id=\"green-visa-work-permit\"><b>Green Visa Work Permit</b></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The </span><b>Green Visa</b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> is designed for skilled professionals, freelancers, and independent workers. </span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">It allows individuals to live and work in the UAE without direct employer sponsorship. This visa typically offers </span><b>5-year residency</b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.</span></p>\n<h3 id=\"temporary-work-permit\"><b>Temporary Work Permit</b></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A temporary work permit is issued for short-term employment or project-based work. </span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">It allows workers to complete specific tasks for a limited period.</span></p>\n<h3 id=\"part-time-work-permit\"><b>Part-Time Work Permit</b></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">This permit allows employees to work for </span><b>multiple employers</b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> at the same time. </span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Many professionals use it for flexible or secondary employment.</span></p>\n<h3 id=\"freelance-work-permit\"><b>Freelance Work Permit</b></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The freelance permit is ideal for independent professionals such as designers, consultants, and media specialists. </span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">It allows individuals to work independently without being tied to one company.</span></p>\n<h3 id=\"mission-work-permit\"><b>Mission Work Permit</b></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A </span><b>mission work permit</b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> is issued for temporary assignments in the UAE. </span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">It is usually valid for </span><b>90 days</b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> and is commonly used for short-term projects.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"eligibility-criteria-for-uae-work-permit\"><b>Eligibility Criteria for UAE Work Permit</b></h2>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Applicants must meet certain </span><b>UAE work visa requirements</b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> before they can obtain a work permit.</span></p>\n<h3 id=\"minimum-age-requirement\"><b>Minimum Age Requirement</b></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Applicants must be </span><b>at least 18 years old</b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> to legally work in the UAE.</span></p>\n<h3 id=\"educational-qualifications\"><b>Educational Qualifications</b></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Educational requirements depend on the job position. Some roles require a university degree or professional certification.</span></p>\n<h3 id=\"valid-job-offer\"><b>Valid Job Offer</b></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The applicant must have a confirmed job offer from a UAE employer along with an official employment contract.</span></p>\n<h3 id=\"medical-fitness-test\"><b>Medical Fitness Test</b></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">All workers must pass a </span><b>government medical fitness test</b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> after arriving in the UAE. This screening checks for certain infectious diseases.</span></p>\n<p><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-9967\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Group-320-1-1024x259-1.webp\" alt=\"\" width=\"1024\" height=\"259\"><noscript><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-9967\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Group-320-1-1024x259-1.webp\" alt=\"\" width=\"1024\" height=\"259\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Group-320-1-1024x259-1.webp 1024w, /wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Group-320-1-1024x259-1-300x76.webp 300w, /wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Group-320-1-1024x259-1-768x194.webp 768w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\"></noscript></p>\n<h2 id=\"documents-required-for-work-permit-in-uae\"><b>Documents Required for Work Permit in UAE</b></h2>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Both the employee and employer must submit specific </span><b>documents for UAE work permit</b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> approval.</span></p>\n<h3 id=\"employee-documents\"><b>Employee Documents</b></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Applicants must usually provide:</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Passport copy (minimum 6 months validity)</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br></span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Passport-size photograph</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br></span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Educational certificates</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br></span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Previous experience letters</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br></span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Signed employment contract</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br></span></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"employer-documents\"><b>Employer Documents</b></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The employer must submit:</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Company trade license</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br></span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Establishment card</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br></span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Employment contract</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br></span></li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Company registration details</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br></span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Providing accurate documents helps avoid delays in the work permit process.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"step-by-step-process-to-apply-for-work-permit-in-uae\"><b>Step-by-Step Process to Apply for Work Permit in UAE</b></h2>\n<h3 id=\"step-1-job-offer-from-uae-employer\"><b>Step 1: Job Offer from UAE Employer</b></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The process begins when a UAE company offers a job to a foreign worker. The employer issues an official offer letter.</span></p>\n<h3 id=\"step-2-work-permit-application\"><b>Step 2: Work Permit Application</b></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The employer submits the work permit application through the labour portal of the Ministry of Human Resources and Emiratisation.</span></p>\n<h3 id=\"step-3-entry-permit-issuance\"><b>Step 3: Entry Permit Issuance</b></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">After approval, the immigration authority issues an entry permit that allows the employee to enter the UAE.</span></p>\n<h3 id=\"step-4-medical-fitness-test\"><b>Step 4: Medical Fitness Test</b></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Once in the country, the employee must complete a government medical screening.</span></p>\n<h3 id=\"step-5-emirates-id-application\"><b>Step 5: Emirates ID Application</b></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The worker registers biometric data for the Emirates ID card.</span></p>\n<h3 id=\"step-6-residence-visa-stamping\"><b>Step 6: Residence Visa Stamping</b></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Finally, the residence visa is stamped in the passport, allowing the employee to legally live and work in the UAE.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"work-permit-cost-in-uae\"><b>Work Permit Cost in UAE</b></h2>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The </span><b>UAE work permit cost</b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> varies depending on the company category and type of permit.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Typical government fees include:</span></p>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><b>Service</b></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><b>Estimated Cost</b></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Work permit approval</span></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">AED 250 – AED 3450</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Entry permit</span></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">AED 300 – AED 1200</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Medical test</span></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">AED 300 – AED 750</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Emirates ID</span></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">AED 270 – AED 370</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">In most cases, the </span><b>total employment visa cost in UAE</b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> ranges between </span><b>AED 3500 and AED 8000</b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">In many companies, employers usually cover these costs as part of the hiring process.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"processing-time-for-uae-work-permit\"><b>Processing Time for UAE Work Permit</b></h2>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The </span><b>UAE work permit processing time</b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> depends on document verification and government approvals.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Typical timeline:</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Work permit approval: </span><b>2–5 days</b><b><br></b></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Entry permit issuance: </span><b>3–7 days</b><b><br></b></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Medical test and Emirates ID: </span><b>2–5 days</b><b><br></b></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Visa stamping: </span><b>3–10 days</b><b><br></b></li>\n</ul>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Overall, the complete process usually takes </span><b>10 to 21 working days</b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"free-zone-vs-mainland-work-permits\"><b>Free Zone vs Mainland Work Permits</b></h2>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The UAE has two main business structures for employment: </span><b>mainland companies</b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> and </span><b>free zone companies</b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Mainland work permits are regulated by the Ministry of Human Resources and Emiratisation. Employees working for mainland companies can work anywhere in the UAE.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Free zone work permits are issued by the specific free zone authority. These permits allow employees to work within that particular free zone.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Each structure has its own rules, visa quotas, and business regulations.</span></p>\n<p><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter size-large wp-image-9966\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Work-permit-UAE-e1773655459277-1024x1006.webp\" alt=\"Work Permit in UAE\" width=\"1024\" height=\"1006\"><noscript><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter size-large wp-image-9966\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Work-permit-UAE-e1773655459277-1024x1006.webp\" alt=\"Work Permit in UAE\" width=\"1024\" height=\"1006\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Work-permit-UAE-e1773655459277-1024x1006.webp 1024w, /wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Work-permit-UAE-e1773655459277-300x295.webp 300w, /wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Work-permit-UAE-e1773655459277-768x754.webp 768w, /wp-content/uploads/2023/03/Work-permit-UAE-e1773655459277.webp 1280w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\"></noscript></p>\n<h2 id=\"how-to-renew-or-cancel-a-uae-work-permit\"><b>How to Renew or Cancel a UAE Work Permit</b></h2>\n<h3 id=\"work-permit-renewal\"><b>Work Permit Renewal</b></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Most UAE work permits must be renewed every </span><b>2 to 3 years</b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The employer usually handles the renewal process and must apply before the visa expires to avoid fines.</span></p>\n<h3 id=\"work-permit-cancellation\"><b>Work Permit Cancellation</b></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If an employee resigns or changes jobs, the employer must cancel the existing permit.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">After cancellation, the employee usually receives a </span><b>grace period</b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> to leave the UAE or transfer to a new employer.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"benefits-of-having-a-uae-work-permit\"><b>Benefits of Having a UAE Work Permit</b></h2>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Having a legal work permit provides several important advantages.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Key </span><b>benefits of working in UAE</b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> include:</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Legal employment status</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Protection under UAE labour laws</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Ability to sponsor family members</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Access to banking services</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Eligibility to rent housing</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Access to healthcare and government services</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br></span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">These benefits make the UAE one of the most attractive destinations for international professionals.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"common-reasons-for-work-permit-rejection\"><b>Common Reasons for Work Permit Rejection</b></h2>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Sometimes, a </span><b>UAE work visa rejection</b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> can occur due to several reasons.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Common causes include:</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Incomplete or incorrect documents</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Company labour violations</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Medical test failure</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Passport validity issues</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Errors in the employment contract</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br></span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Ensuring that all documents are correct can significantly reduce the risk of rejection.</span></p>\n<h2 id=\"faqs-about-work-permit-in-uae\"><b>FAQs About Work Permit in UAE</b></h2>\n<h3 id=\"1-how-long-does-it-take-to-get-a-work-permit-in-uae\"><b>1. How long does it take to get a work permit in UAE?</b></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Most applications are processed within </span><b>10 to 21 working days</b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, depending on approvals and document verification.</span></p>\n<h3 id=\"2-who-pays-for-the-uae-work-permit\"><b>2. Who pays for the UAE work permit?</b></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">In most cases, </span><b>the employer pays the work permit and visa costs</b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> as part of the recruitment process.</span></p>\n<h3 id=\"3-can-i-work-in-uae-without-a-work-permit\"><b>3. Can I work in UAE without a work permit?</b></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">No. Working without a valid permit is illegal and can lead to </span><b>fines, deportation, and employment bans</b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.</span></p>\n<h3 id=\"4-can-a-tourist-visa-convert-to-a-work-permit\"><b>4. Can a tourist visa convert to a work permit?</b></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Yes. If a person receives a job offer while on a tourist visa, the employer can apply for a work permit and change the visa status legally.</span></p>\n<h3 id=\"5-how-long-is-a-uae-work-permit-valid\"><b>5. How long is a UAE work permit valid?</b></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Most standard permits are valid for </span><b>2 years</b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, although some visa categories, such as the Green Visa, may last longer.</span></p>\n<h3 id=\"6-can-i-change-jobs-with-a-uae-work-permit\"><b>6. Can I change jobs with a UAE work permit?</b></h3>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Yes. Employees can change jobs after their current employer cancels the existing work permit and a new employer applies for a new one.</span></p>\n<p><script type=\"application/ld+json\">\n{\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n  \"@type\": \"FAQPage\",\n  \"mainEntity\": [{\n    \"@type\": \"Question\",\n    \"name\": \"How long does it take to get a work permit in UAE?\",\n    \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n      \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n      \"text\": \"Most applications are processed within 10 to 21 working days, depending on approvals and document verification.\"\n    }\n  },{\n    \"@type\": \"Question\",\n    \"name\": \"Who pays for the UAE work permit?\",\n    \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n      \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n      \"text\": \"In most cases, the employer pays the work permit and visa costs as part of the recruitment process.\"\n    }\n  },{\n    \"@type\": \"Question\",\n    \"name\": \"Can I work in UAE without a work permit?\",\n    \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n      \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n      \"text\": \"No. Working without a valid permit is illegal and can lead to fines, deportation, and employment bans.\"\n    }\n  },{\n    \"@type\": \"Question\",\n    \"name\": \"Can a tourist visa convert to a work permit?\",\n    \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n      \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n      \"text\": \"Yes. If a person receives a job offer while on a tourist visa, the employer can apply for a work permit and change the visa status legally.\"\n    }\n  },{\n    \"@type\": \"Question\",\n    \"name\": \"How long is a UAE work permit valid?\",\n    \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n      \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n      \"text\": \"Most standard permits are valid for 2 years, although some visa categories, such as the Green Visa, may last longer.\"\n    }\n  },{\n    \"@type\": \"Question\",\n    \"name\": \"Can I change jobs with a UAE work permit?\",\n    \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n      \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n      \"text\": \"Yes. Employees can change jobs after their current employer cancels the existing work permit and a new employer applies for a new one.\"\n    }\n  }]\n}\n</script></p><!-- Simple Share Buttons Adder (8.5.6) simplesharebuttons.com --><div class=\"ssba-modern-2 ssba ssbp-wrap aligncenter ssbp--theme-8\"><div style=\"text-align:center\"><ul class=\"ssbp-list\"><li class=\"ssbp-li--facebook\"><a data-site=\"facebook\" class=\"ssba_facebook_share ssba_share_link ssbp-facebook ssbp-btn\" href=\"https://www.facebook.com/sharer.php?t=The%20Process%20Involved%20In%20Work%20Permit%20In%20UAE%202026:%20Complete%20Guide&amp;u=/work-permit-in-uae/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"color:#4267B2; background-color: #4267B2; height: 48px; width: 48px; \"><span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"#fff\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\" height=\"1em\" width=\"1em\" viewBox=\"0 0 40 40\">\n  <g>\n    <path d=\"m21.7 16.7h5v5h-5v11.6h-5v-11.6h-5v-5h5v-2.1c0-2 0.6-4.5 1.8-5.9 1.3-1.3 2.8-2 4.7-2h3.5v5h-3.5c-0.9 0-1.5 0.6-1.5 1.5v3.5z\"></path>\n  </g>\n</svg>\n\n</span><span class=\"color-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"28\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 28\">\n  <path fill=\"#3B5998\" d=\"M10.7,10.7 L15.7,10.7 L15.7,15.7 L10.7,15.7 L10.7,27.3 L5.7,27.3 L5.7,15.7 L0.7,15.7 L0.7,10.7 L5.7,10.7 L5.7,8.6 C5.7,6.6 6.3,4.1 7.5,2.7 C8.8,1.4 10.3,0.7 12.2,0.7 L15.7,0.7 L15.7,5.7 L12.2,5.7 C11.3,5.7 10.7,6.3 10.7,7.2 L10.7,10.7 Z\"></path>\n</svg>\n</span><div title=\"Facebook\" class=\"ssbp-text\">Facebook</div></a></li><li class=\"ssbp-li--twitter\"><a data-site=\"twitter\" class=\"ssba_twitter_share ssba_share_link ssbp-twitter ssbp-btn\" href=\"https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=The%20Process%20Involved%20In%20Work%20Permit%20In%20UAE%202026:%20Complete%20Guide&amp;url=/work-permit-in-uae/&amp;via=\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"color:#000000; background-color: #000000; height: 48px; width: 48px; \"><span><svg width=\"25\" height=\"25\" viewBox=\"0 0 25 25\" fill=\"none\" xmlns